summary: MLS Enforcing-Mode Boot Validation (COPR-based validation of PR #3380, EXPERIMENTAL)
description: |
    EXPERIMENTAL sibling of tmt/mls-final.fmf (same directory). Validates
    upstream PR #3380
    (https://github.com/fedora-selinux/selinux-policy/pull/3380, "Enable
    cloud-init under MLS", 2 commits: the cloud-init fix + the udev_t
    MLS-boot-hang fix) as the REAL Packit/COPR-built selinux-policy-mls
    RPM package, instead of manually building/loading standalone .te
    modules on top of an unpatched package.

    Enables the Packit-managed COPR repo
    packit/fedora-selinux-selinux-policy-3380 (confirmed via the GitHub
    API against PR #3380 HEAD c3fbc760b9: rpm-build succeeded for
    fedora-44-x86_64, fedora-45-x86_64 and fedora-rawhide-x86_64) before
    installing selinux-policy-mls. Since dnf/dnf5 picks the highest EVR
    across ALL enabled repos (not just the newly-enabled one), and a
    fast-moving compose can already have a newer selinux-policy-mls build
    than Packit's PR snapshot (observed live on Fedora-Rawhide), the
    prepare script pins the exact NVR Packit built for PR #3380 on the
    fedora-44-x86_64 chroot -- so run this plan against --compose
    Fedora-44, not Fedora-Rawhide.

    This covers 6 of the 8 modules the production plan builds locally
    (cloudform + the 5 udev_t fixes now folded into udev.te upstream);
    mlssshpipes and udevptrace are NOT part of PR #3380 (not present
    anywhere in its diff) and are still built/loaded locally here.

    This is a one-off validation test, NOT a replacement for the
    production tmt/mls-final.fmf plan/mechanism. Do not treat a pass here
    as a reason to change mls-final.fmf without a separate, explicit
    decision to do so.

    Requires environment variable PR_NUMBER (the selinux-policy PR number
    whose Packit-managed COPR build, packit/fedora-selinux-selinux-policy-
    ${PR_NUMBER}, should be installed from). Defaults to 3380 below for
    manual/ad-hoc runs; a CI caller (e.g. `testing-farm request`) should
    override it with `-e PR_NUMBER=<n>` / `--tmt-environment PR_NUMBER=<n>`
    for whichever PR is actually under test.

    In addition to the boot/cloud-init/AVC check above, this plan also
    discovers and runs the real, canonical
    https://github.com/SELinuxProject/selinux-testsuite against this same
    MLS-enforcing, COPR-validated guest (see the second `discover` phase
    below) -- this repo's own tmt/plans.fmf `/ci` plan already wires up
    that same upstream testsuite via `how: fmf`, but only for a *separate*
    validation track: targeted policy + SELinux userspace rebuilt from
    this git checkout (STS_ROOT_DOMAIN: unconfined_t). That track is
    orthogonal to this plan (stock Fedora userspace + the COPR-built
    selinux-policy-mls RPM under test), so instead of reusing it as-is
    this plan adds its own `fmf` discover phase, without the
    /prepare-selinux-userspace build-from-git step (irrelevant here --
    we're validating the shipped RPM policy, not this checkout's
    userspace), and with STS_ROOT_DOMAIN set to sysadm_t instead of
    unconfined_t.

    sysadm_t (not unconfined_t) is the right root domain for MLS: this
    plan's own prepare script already turns on the `ssh_sysadm_login`
    boolean (needed for root's SSH session, which maps to
    sysadm_u:sysadm_r:sysadm_t under MLS, to transition out of
    sshd_session_t at all -- see mls-final-copr-prepare.sh). MLS/strict
    policy has no unconfined_t. STS_ROOT_DOMAIN=sysadm_t is itself an
    upstream-supported, CI-tested value (selinux-testsuite's own
    .github/workflows/checks.yml matrix runs `domain: [unconfined_t,
    sysadm_t]`), and runtests.pl explicitly accepts running as root in
    sysadm_r (`$role ne "sysadm_r" && $role ne "unconfined_r" && $role ne
    "system_r"`). The testsuite is also directly MLS-aware, not just
    targeted/MCS-oriented: it auto-detects the running policy type via
    its own tests/pol_detect (NON-MLS/MCS/MLS, based on the kernel's
    initial SID level) and both tests/Makefile and policy/Makefile branch
    on that ($(POL_TYPE) = MLS/MCS) to build extra MLS/MCS-only test
    modules (test_glblub.cil for MLS, plus test_add_levels.cil for MCS)
    on top of the always-built test_mlsconstrain.cil -- i.e. it ships
    real, dedicated MLS test coverage, not something bolted on. The test
    policy itself is just semodule-loaded on top of whatever base policy
    is already active, so it does not assume/require targeted policy.

    The testsuite's own tmt/plans.fmf `/prepare-system` test (order: 1)
    only runs its STS_ROOT_DOMAIN/STS_KERNEL setup (and a possible
    tmt-reboot) when `$TMT_REBOOT_COUNT -eq 0`; since this plan's own
    prepare step already consumed 2 reboots switching to MLS+Enforcing
    before execute even starts, that setup is a no-op here by the time
    it runs -- harmless, since the sysadm_login boolean is already on
    from this plan's own prepare script and MLS's root login already
    maps to sysadm_u by default. Same filter as the existing `/ci` plan
    (`tag:-ci & tag:-nfs`): excludes the CI-only meta-tests (`/avc-check`,
    `/gitignore-coverage`) and the NFS subtest, which need infrastructure
    (a real nfs-server, git checkout cleanliness) irrelevant to this VM.
    Not filtered: `/unprepare`'s STS_ROOT_DOMAIN=sysadm_t branch tries to
    revert root's login mapping to `unconfined_u` at the very end, which
    likely does not exist under MLS -- if that harmless cleanup step
    fails/errors, it does not affect the actual regression test results
    above it.

environment:
  PR_NUMBER: "3380"
  # See the description above: sysadm_t (not unconfined_t) is the correct
  # root domain for an MLS guest, and matches this plan's own prepare
  # script (ssh_sysadm_login boolean already on). STS_KERNEL is a no-op
  # here (see above) but set explicitly for documentation purposes.
  STS_ROOT_DOMAIN: sysadm_t
  STS_KERNEL: default

prepare:
  - name: Install MLS policy from PR #3380's COPR build, build/load the 2 remaining local fixes, switch to MLS and then Enforcing (2 reboots)
    how: shell
    script: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-final-copr-prepare.sh

discover:
  - name: mls-boot-cloudinit
    how: shell
    tests:
      - name: /mls-boot-cloudinit-avc-check
        summary: Confirm cloud-init completed under cloud_init_t on the MLS-enforcing COPR guest; dump AVC denials informationally
        # Must run before the selinux-testsuite's own /prepare-system
        # (order: 1 below), which unconditionally truncates
        # /var/log/audit/audit.log -- running any later would erase the
        # boot-time AVC evidence this check depends on.
        order: 0
        duration: 10m
        test: $TMT_TREE/tmt/mls-final-copr-execute.sh
  - name: selinux-testsuite
    how: fmf
    url: https://github.com/SELinuxProject/selinux-testsuite
    ref: main
    filter: tag:-ci & tag:-nfs

execute:
  how: tmt
